    Clerk: candidate correction for B6 -- remove self-referential bill digest annotation
    
    records/bills/executive-innovation-office-act.md carried a line
    '**Digest (current):** 647449cc...'. Because the line is part of the hashed
    file, the bill's SHA-256 can never equal the digest it declares; every
    non-quarantined ballot row for this bill (all 10 seats, all 'yes') records
    647449cc..., the digest of the same text WITHOUT that annotation
    (blob at commit 08e03c3).
    
    Removing only the two annotation lines restores the file byte-for-byte to the
    text the ballots hashed (sha256 647449cc...), so:
      - tests/ballot-integrity.sh: PASS (rc 0)
      - government/tally.sh executive-innovation-office-act: PASSED (10/10 yes)
    
    This changes no operative provision and no vote. It is a CANDIDATE correction
    only: not merged, pending independent exact-commit review and Act 21 exact-tree
    green evidence. It resolves only the ballot-record digest mismatch. It does NOT
    establish Act 24 enactment validity: the LAWS.md heading was rewritten to
    'enacted' at '2026-10-31T06:XXZ' (placeholder minute) by commit 7396f907, and
    the bill's own status line still reads 'proposed, NOT ENACTED'. Recorded in
    records/investigations/innovation-office-integration-determination-20261108.md (B6).

